= Win Over the Soldiers

The soldiers and the police are workers' sons too, most of them. Their officers keep them in barracks and feed them stories about Bolshevik murderers. If even a few companies refuse to march, the whole balance of the week changes.

- @leaflets: Smuggle leaflets into the barracks.
- @fraternise: Send the women and the young to the checkpoints.
- @deserters: Offer shelter to deserters who bring their weapons.

@leaflets
subtitle: Some soldiers waver. Those caught with our leaflets are court-martialled.
on-arrival: army_loyalty -= 3; police_loyalty -= 2; crisis_momentum += 4; repression += 3

The leaflets are tucked into bread deliveries and laundry bundles. In one barracks, the men refuse to clean their rifles.

@fraternise
subtitle: Hard to shoot at people who brought you coffee. A little goodwill on both sides.
on-arrival: army_loyalty -= 2; crisis_momentum += 3; worker_support += 1

Women from the workers' districts bring coffee and cigarettes to the boys at the roadblocks, and talk to them about their mothers.

@deserters
subtitle: A few more rifles, and a few more trained men. The officers will want revenge.
on-arrival: red_guards_arms += 3; red_guards_strength += 0.3; army_loyalty -= 1; crisis_momentum += 2; repression += 2; lean_offensive += 1

A handful of soldiers walk out of the barracks at night with their rifles and their ammunition belts. Our people hide them in allotment huts.
